.TH "PB-ENV-TEAM-GRANT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-team-grant - Grant an account access to an encrypted ENV team scope


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env team grant <team> <account> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Grant an account access to an encrypted ENV team scope

.PP
Give one account access to the selected encrypted team ENV scope. The account must still accept and reconcile its grant before using values.

.PP
Team ENV scopes have their own encrypted keys and explicit account grants. Rotation preserves values while replacing access keys; reset discards values. Review the confirmation and affected members before changing custody.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for grant

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-team(1)\fP
